      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-16T22:07:52Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(3d): prevent shared-depth XY crossings in adaptive microlifts, helices, and offset shells\n\nLand `helix_about`'s final half-turn on exact `z1` so small decimal\nstepdowns (e.g. 0.15 mm) do not leave a 1-ULP ramp overlapping the next\nlevel's descending helix.\n\nScale `microlift::link_at` heights strictly below the nearest earlier\nhorizontal cut plane above `z`, probe candidate return feeds against\nprior `Feed` moves via `machining2d::arc_cross`, promote a crossing low\nreturn to a `high: true` down-only ramp when clear, and fall back to a\n`hop_z` rapid plus `Plunge` retract when even `down` crosses or the gap\nis <= 0.02 mm.\n\nProtect 3-D offset shells by probing `descent::push_helix` against\nalready-posted `b.moves()` (re-placing around `along_pass`/`dive_room`\nor falling back when needed) and hopping over any `level_ctx::feed_leg`\nchord that would cross an earlier cut at shared depth or Z band.\n\nPins: `helix_about_exact_end_z_prevents_next_level_ulp_crossing`,\n`microlift_link_stays_below_prior_level_and_avoids_entry_crossings`,\n`adaptive_small_stepdown_microlift_and_helix_stay_crossing_free`, and\n`offset_shell_fillet_helix_and_floor_never_cross`.\n\nFixes #2237\n\nCo-Authored-By: Antigravity <noreply@google.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "b30553422d4fbde7ddf06e08c066a1c6281d5b46",
